    "notes": [
      "Baseline numbers for tools/perf/compare_baseline.py. Updated by maintainers (run_perf_ci.sh --update-baseline) when an intentional optimisation or regression is accepted.",
      "All timing values are seconds (matches harness output). compare_baseline.py converts to milliseconds for display.",
      "NOT a CI gate. This suite is run manually/occasionally (e.g. around a major release) on the maintainer's box; baseline is calibrated to that hardware and is NOT comparable to GitHub-runner numbers. See tools/perf/run_perf_ci.sh header.",
      "Re-captured 2026-06-07 (P1a): min-of-7 timing (the minimum of 7 reps + 1 warmup, per op) in all three harnesses, at n=100000 (10x the prior 10000). ref_diff/name_tokenized measure the v2 codecs (not comparable to pre-2026-06 v1 numbers).",
      "regression_threshold_pct tightened 50 -> 15 (P1a): min-of-N + 10x workload cut back-to-back drift on the compute/transport/codec paths to <=8.5%. Two drift runs measured 2026-06-07; full rationale in docs/benchmarks/2026-06-07-perf-min-of-n.md.",
      "min_abs_ms=5.0: sub-5ms metrics swing +100-266% on pure jitter; the floor reports but never fails a metric when BOTH baseline and new are below it (a sub-floor->above-floor jump still fails).",
      "metric_overrides: per-metric thresholds for the few inherently-noisy metrics so the tight global gate still applies to everything else. ms.sqlite.write (~15%, fsync) and codecs.rans_o1_decode (~17%) get 30%. jcamp.compressed_read (~4-6ms) straddles the 5ms floor and jitters ~48% across the boundary -> 60%.",
      "(P1e) parity_ratio_threshold + parity_allow drive tools/perf/check_parity.py, the cross-SDK perf-parity detector. ratio=max(ms)/min(ms) across python/java/objc; metrics whose fastest SDK is below min_abs_ms are below-floor (never flag); parity_allow names known-legit gaps (different mechanism/backend). The currently-flagged genuine concerns (streaming.write/read, transport.plain.encode, codecs.genomic.delta_rans_*, genomic.read) are deliberately NOT allow-listed \u2014 see docs/benchmarks/2026-06-07-perf-xsdk-parity.md, they become follow-up issues.",
      "(P1d) encryption.genomic: the original '3.7ms/10MB impossible' premise was WRONG (that is ~5 GB/s AES-NI, correct). Payload scaled 10 MiB -> 64 MiB to lift it above the 5ms floor. Result: Python/ObjC encrypt+decrypt are now stable (<5% drift) BUT Java still swings +/-100% (encrypt 85<->174ms, decrypt +46%) because the Java path's javax.crypto Cipher.getInstance runs inside the timed call (provider lookup + JIT) plus 64 MiB GC churn -- a product-code issue (hoist getInstance in EncryptionManager) tracked as a follow-up. metric_overrides is per-metric-key (not per-SDK), so encryption.genomic.encrypt/decrypt are set report-only (1000) for all SDKs; a per-SDK override would let Python/ObjC stay gated -- also a follow-up."
    ]
  },
